{
  "name": "rust-core_io",
  "description": "A specialized compatibility layer that backports the Rust standard library's I/O module to no_std environments by extracting and patching upstream libstd source code. It provides core abstractions such as the Read and Write traits, stripping away operating system dependencies while maintaining feature-gated support for alloc and collections. The project employs a robust build-time version mapping system to ensure binary and source compatibility with specific nightly compiler toolchains.",
